# The setup screen names the token command and the HTTPS requirement before
# anything has failed, and the address field takes typed input.
wait-for Home Panel
wait-for kobo connect homepanel
expect must be on HTTPS
clean
shot homepanel-setup
tap Check again
wait-for No address has arrived
clean
shot homepanel-check-again
tap-id home-url
wait-for Home Assistant address
type homeassistant
expect https://homeassistant
clean
shot homepanel-typed
# Home Assistant needs HTTPS, so a plain address stays in the field with the
# reason under it rather than being saved.
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
type ha.local
tap Test connection
wait-for Use an https:// Home Assistant URL.
expect ha.local
expect-missing Testing connection
clean
shot homepanel-wrong-scheme
# An HTTPS address is saved and tested. With no token on the reader the
# test says which command brings one, and setup stays.
tap-id home-url
wait-for Home Assistant address
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
tap Delete character
type https://ha.example.net
tap Test connection
wait-for No Home Assistant account is on this reader yet
expect Connect Home Assistant
expect https://ha.example.net
clean
shot homepanel-no-token
# Use phone shows the profile page where tokens are made, as a code, and
# Edit address goes back to the field.
tap Use phone
wait-for https://ha.example.net/profile/security
expect long-lived access tokens are made
clean
shot homepanel-phone
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Connect Home Assistant
expect Use phone
tap Use phone
wait-for https://ha.example.net/profile/security
tap Edit address
wait-for Test connection
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Connect Home Assistant
# The address was saved, so the next start opens the panel, empty.
restart
wait-for No tiles
expect Add a Home Assistant device.
expect-missing Connect Home Assistant
expect-missing Not connected yet.
clean
shot homepanel-empty-grid
# Adding a tile asks Home Assistant for its devices. Without a token that
# fails in words, and the picker stays open on adding a device by its ID.
tap Add tile
wait-for No Home Assistant account is on this reader yet
expect Add a device by its ID
clean
shot homepanel-add-no-token
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for No tiles
# Settings: the saved address, the wall panel switch and the tile count.
tap Settings
wait-for Wall panel
expect https://ha.example.net
expect Two tiles per row.
expect 0 of 12
clean
shot homepanel-settings-empty
tap Edit tiles
wait-for Add a tile first.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Wall panel
tap Wall panel
wait-for One large tile per row, for a reader by the door.
clean
shot homepanel-wall-on
# The switch is kept across a restart.
restart
wait-for No tiles
tap Settings
wait-for One large tile per row, for a reader by the door.
tap Wall panel
wait-for Two tiles per row.
# Tapping the address opens setup with it in the field; back returns.
tap https://ha.example.net
wait-for Connect Home Assistant
expect https://ha.example.net
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for No tiles
